; Engine configuration file.
; DubSar Theater — EnkiDDB HeptaScript Notebook & Grid/Orbit Viewer
; BahyWay.Ecosystem v4.0
;
; PB-207 (2026-07-19): this file did not exist before -- every scene and
; script in this directory was real and complete, but nothing was
; openable in the Godot editor. Main scene is main_theater.tscn (the
; DubSar Theater shell); press Ctrl+E once running to open the
; HeptaScript Editor overlay (scenes/heptascript_editor.tscn), which is
; the actual "notebook" -- CodeEdit for QUERY:/SEARCH: HeptaScript, a
; live execution log showing real row content (not just counts), a NODE
; target picker defaulting to EnkiDDB, and a PDM tab that renders results
; as a GEM/ORBIT/FUZZY particle-classification grid.
;
; The 3D BIGRING particle ring in main_theater.tscn (the CENTER_STAGE
; backdrop) is real geometry but is NOT wired to live query results --
; that would require a Rust GDExtension (BigRingNode3D) that was only
; ever referenced in a code comment, never built as a compiled crate in
; this repo. Treat it as atmospheric only.
;
; PB-217 (2026-07-20): two real, working ways to inspect live EnkiDDB/
; EnkiMDB data now exist -- Ctrl+E opens the HeptaScript Editor overlay
; (CodeEdit + execution log + NODE picker + PDM tab), and Ctrl+G opens
; the Grid & Orbit 3D view (scenes/theater_3d.tscn, a full scene switch,
; Escape to return) -- real particles from a real query, grouped into
; rings by their real category (meta.collection / artifact.kind), not
; the CENTER_STAGE backdrop described above.
;
; PB-218/219 (2026-07-20): Ctrl+K opens the Graph Explorer overlay
; (scenes/graph_explorer.tscn) -- a GraphEdit view of real link.target/
; link.description particles (emit_link, reused by emit_sections'
; "section-of" and emit_concept_mentions' "mentioned-in"), built from an
; exact meta.title QUERY. Fixed a real serialization bug in
; enkiddb-read-server/enkimdb-read-server's fmt_val() first (KakiPk values
; were falling through to Rust's Debug format instead of hex), live-
; verified locally before writing any of this scene's code.
;
; 2026-07-21: Ctrl+D opens the New DubSar Theater dashboard shell
; (scenes/dashboard_theater.tscn) -- a tabbed 2D Monitor Dashboard for
; all 7 EnkiDB Types (EnkiDB, EnkiDW, EnkiSDB, EnkiODB, EnkiQDB, EnkiMDB,
; EnkiDDB), each tab driven by a real, schema-agnostic probe query
; against that engine's real Read Node. Lives side by side with the 3D
; theater as an alternative mode -- a header button and Escape both
; return to this scene, neither replaces the other. Also fixed a real
; regression in the same commit: sumuukin_client.gd (the shared fan-out
; client heptascript_editor.gd/pdm_tab.gd/graph_explorer.gd all use) was
; still speaking the old JSON protocol against a server shape no real
; Read Node answers anymore -- rewritten to the same binary wire
; theater_3d.gd's EnkiDB target already proved, and theater_3d.gd itself
; now shares that one decoder instead of keeping a second, half-migrated
; copy (its EnkiDDB/EnkiMDB targets had silently regressed to the JSON
; path earlier the same day this session upgraded those two read-servers
; off JSON).
;
; 2026-07-21: Ctrl+O opens the Onion Layers 3D Tower (scenes/onion_tower_3d.
; tscn) -- the same real 25-layer/163-crate dataset as the sealed 2D onion
; artifact (docs/BAHYWAY_ONION_LAYERS.html, transcribed verbatim from
; workspace/bahyway_v4/Cargo.toml), rendered as a stacked, mouse-orbit,
; click-to-inspect 3D tower instead of nested flat circles. Full scene
; switch (owns its own Camera3D), Escape returns here. No GA/simplicial-
; complex node type was added to the PDM Node Graph editor in the same
; work -- see scripts/pdm_node_graph.gd's header for why (real Rust
; implementations exist but have no GDExtension bridge into Godot yet).
;
; 2026-07-22: config/icon added -- the BahyWay "B / road" mark (icon.svg,
; the Architect's own vector source) replaces the default Godot Engine
; icon as this project's window/taskbar icon. Note: this ONLY takes
; effect when the project is actually RUN (`godot --path ...`, no
; --editor flag) -- the Godot EDITOR's own window always shows the Godot
; Engine icon regardless of this setting, because that icon belongs to
; the editor application itself, not to any project it has open. This is
; exactly why PB-226 (playbooks/playbook_226_launch_dubsar_godot_ide.yml)
; now defaults to run mode instead of editor mode.
;
; 2026-07-22 (same day, second gap found): config/icon controls the
; WINDOW icon only. It does NOT control Godot's own boot splash -- the
; "GODOT / Game engine" mascot screen the engine shows for a moment while
; it initializes, BEFORE run/main_scene is ever reached. That splash is a
; separate, compiled-in engine resource, governed by its own
; boot_splash/* settings below -- config/icon alone can never remove it.
; Disabled outright (show_image=false) rather than replaced with a
; branded splash image, because the Architect's law is that a stakeholder
; must see NOTHING but the login popup, triggered the instant Godot
; starts -- not even a branded flash screen first. bg_color is set to
; DubSarTheme.BG (#0a0e1a) so the one unavoidable blank frame before
; login.tscn paints matches the app's own background instead of Godot's
; default blue.

config_version=5

[application]

config/name="BahyWay.Ecosystem v4.0 — DubSar Theater IDE"
config/description="EnkiDDB HeptaScript Notebook -- inspect real ingested BahyWay.Ecosystem v4.0 documentation and test semantic (vector) search against a live EnkiDDB Read Node."
run/main_scene="res://scenes/login.tscn"
config/icon="res://icon.svg"
config/features=PackedStringArray("4.3", "Forward Plus")
boot_splash/show_image=false
boot_splash/bg_color=Color(0.0392157, 0.0549020, 0.1019608, 1)

[display]

; FIXED (2026-07-27): no [display] section existed at all, so this ran
; at Godot's small default window size (1152x648). The EnkiDB Connector
; Wizard's Page 1 (7 database cards in a grid) plus its header/step-
; indicator/footer overflows that easily, pushing the Next/Prev buttons
; below the visible window with no scrollbar to reach them -- confirmed
; live: the Architect's remote viewer has no zoom/resize controls at
; all, so this has to be fixed at the source, not worked around by the
; user resizing the window themselves.
;
; ENLARGED 2026-08-02: same window/size/mode=2 (Maximized) fix applied
; to sargon-passport-manager/gilgamesh-master-key after 1280x900 was
; still reported too small -- kept consistent across all 3 tools.
window/size/viewport_width=1280
window/size/viewport_height=900
window/size/mode=2

; FIXED 2026-08-02, live: mode=2 alone does NOT scale the UI -- confirmed
; live on sargon-passport-manager/gilgamesh-master-key, text stayed tiny
; on a maximized window since Godot doesn't scale UI with window size by
; default. canvas_items stretch scales the whole UI to fill the actual
; window size, using viewport_width/height above as the reference
; resolution. Applied here too for consistency across all 3 tools.
window/stretch/mode="canvas_items"
window/stretch/aspect="expand"

[rendering]

renderer/rendering_method="forward_plus"
